<Base title="Privacy and cookies | Trek Trails" description="What Trek Trails measures about visits to the site, which cookies are used and how to change your choice." path="/privacy/">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="pagehead"><span class="label">Privacy</span><h1>Privacy and cookies</h1></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Trek Trails is a personal, non-commercial website about multi-day walks. It has no accounts, no newsletter and no forms, so it does not ask you for any personal details.</p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>If you choose "Accept" in the cookie banner, the site loads Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics. These place cookies in your browser and send Google information about your visit: the pages you open, how you arrived, your approximate location and the type of device and browser you use. We use this only to see which pages are read and what to improve. It is not used for advertising, and advertising cookies stay switched off.</p>
    <p>If you choose "Decline", or make no choice, no analytics are loaded and no cookies are set.</p>
    <h2>Changing your choice</h2>
    <p>Your choice is stored in your own browser. You can change it at any time with <a href="#" data-cookies>Cookie settings</a>, which is also at the bottom of every page. Clearing your browser data resets it.</p>
    <h2>Other services</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted by Cloudflare, which processes technical data such as IP addresses to deliver pages and protect the site. Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts. Links to other websites, such as Instagram or trip organisers, follow those websites' own privacy policies.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>For questions about your data, send a message to Trek Trails on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/trektrails_org/" rel="noopener">Instagram</a>.</p>
    <p class="fine">Last updated: November 2026.</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Base>
